1
00:00:00,257 --> 00:00:01,925
[singing "Nagisa" by Spitz]

2
00:00:09,182 --> 00:00:11,309
I said this is pretty awesome!

3
00:00:12,894 --> 00:00:15,063
{\an8}[chuckles] Mm-hm.

4
00:00:18,859 --> 00:00:21,445
[Taiki] <i>Why do I feel
like we're getting closer?</i>

5
00:00:22,487 --> 00:00:25,032
[sighs contentedly]

6
00:00:26,992 --> 00:00:29,911
<i>The cultural festival is so fun!</i>

7
00:00:30,537 --> 00:00:31,747
Oh!

8
00:00:32,289 --> 00:00:33,457
Huh?!

9
00:00:36,042 --> 00:00:37,377
[Taiki grunts]

10
00:00:40,338 --> 00:00:42,758
[growling]

11
00:00:44,551 --> 00:00:46,470
[whimpering]

12
00:00:46,553 --> 00:00:48,472
[continues growling]

13
00:00:48,555 --> 00:00:50,474
[continues whimpering]

14
00:00:56,605 --> 00:01:01,026
No!

15
00:01:08,950 --> 00:01:11,369
[Taiki] I knew it,
there's no way I can do this.

16
00:01:11,453 --> 00:01:14,206
[Niina] You're literally in costume.
What are you talking about?

17
00:01:14,289 --> 00:01:16,374
Only 'cause you forced me to put it on!

18
00:01:16,458 --> 00:01:18,877
You're the only one of us who can do it.

19
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:20,879
And the audience is waiting on you.

20
00:01:20,962 --> 00:01:22,130
[Taiki] For a stand-in?

21
00:01:22,214 --> 00:01:23,590
Hey, what about Kyo?

22
00:01:23,673 --> 00:01:25,008
He knows all the lines.

23
00:01:25,967 --> 00:01:27,636
[Niina] He got called to the committee.

24
00:01:27,719 --> 00:01:29,137
[groans]

25
00:01:31,014 --> 00:01:32,390
{\an8}Please, Taiki.

26
00:01:32,474 --> 00:01:34,726
You've watched over the whole production.

27
00:01:35,352 --> 00:01:39,439
Can you please do this, so that
all of our work wasn't for nothing?

28
00:01:41,983 --> 00:01:45,779
[Taiki] <i>I have been here since day one,
and I know how hard they've worked.</i>

29
00:01:48,490 --> 00:01:50,242
[hopeful music playing]

30
00:01:56,915 --> 00:01:58,500
[inaudible]

31
00:02:05,841 --> 00:02:07,926
[Taiki sighs] Okay, fine. I'll do it.

32
00:02:08,009 --> 00:02:09,886
I'll play Prince Charming.

33
00:02:09,970 --> 00:02:11,555
[boy 1] That's what we wanted to hear!

34
00:02:11,638 --> 00:02:14,182
[boy 2] That's real leadership!
We love you!

35
00:02:14,266 --> 00:02:15,267
SNOW WHITE SCRIPT

36
00:02:15,350 --> 00:02:18,520
- [Taiki sighs] Someone get me a script!
- [Niina] Here you go!

37
00:02:18,603 --> 00:02:21,189
[Taiki] If I forget any of my lines,
you back me up!

38
00:02:26,153 --> 00:02:27,237
{\an8}Okay!

39
00:02:28,905 --> 00:02:30,907
[opening theme song playing]

40
00:02:55,223 --> 00:02:58,643
BLUE BOX

41
00:03:58,662 --> 00:04:00,080
{\an8}[all] Let's go! Taiki!

42
00:04:00,163 --> 00:04:02,040
{\an8}EPISODE 20
AS ONE OF HER CLOSEST FRIENDS

43
00:04:02,123 --> 00:04:05,085
[Taiki] <i>Sure. I've seen them
rehearse over and over.</i>

44
00:04:05,168 --> 00:04:08,964
<i>I might not get every word perfect,
but I should know most of the lines.</i>

45
00:04:10,257 --> 00:04:12,008
<i>So I'm gonna be fine.</i>

46
00:04:12,092 --> 00:04:14,469
[distorted noise]

47
00:04:15,095 --> 00:04:17,013
{\an8}<i>Oh, who am I kidding?!</i>

48
00:04:17,597 --> 00:04:19,015
<i>We're talking about me here,</i>

49
00:04:19,099 --> 00:04:22,644
<i>the guy who's only been onstage to
play melodica in a grade school recital!</i>

50
00:04:22,727 --> 00:04:26,481
<i>The guy who can't even say
"She sells she-shells by the..."</i> [screams]

51
00:04:27,107 --> 00:04:30,735
<i>Is this the "unthinkable ordeal"
that Nishida was talking about?</i>

52
00:04:31,403 --> 00:04:33,321
<i>I can just ad-lib the small stuff.</i>

53
00:04:33,405 --> 00:04:36,866
<i>And if I mess up a line,
I can cover it up by singing.</i>

54
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:38,493
<i>Um... and then there's...</i>

55
00:04:38,576 --> 00:04:39,452
KISS

56
00:04:39,536 --> 00:04:40,870
<i>...this little problem.</i>

57
00:04:41,579 --> 00:04:43,039
[breath trembling]

58
00:04:47,127 --> 00:04:49,963
<i>I know, all I need to do is fake it.</i>

59
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:54,509
<i>But it will be impossible for me
not to think of the real thing.</i>

60
00:04:55,468 --> 00:04:56,678
Wanna do it for real?

61
00:04:57,345 --> 00:04:58,680
[sighs]

62
00:04:58,763 --> 00:05:00,765
<i>I can't let it look awkward.</i>

63
00:05:01,683 --> 00:05:03,685
I'll get a seat right in the center.

64
00:05:03,768 --> 00:05:05,186
[exclaims]

65
00:05:05,895 --> 00:05:07,939
[groans]

66
00:05:09,899 --> 00:05:12,193
<i>And Chinatsu's going to be there.</i>

67
00:05:14,195 --> 00:05:16,531
<i>Now it looks like I lied to her again.</i>

68
00:05:18,992 --> 00:05:22,078
{\an8}<i>It's not as if I can ask her not to come.</i>

69
00:05:22,162 --> 00:05:23,455
{\an8}CHINATSU KANO

70
00:05:23,538 --> 00:05:25,707
{\an8}[music ends]

71
00:05:25,790 --> 00:05:27,876
{\an8}- [all applauding]
- [host] Thank you, everyone!

72
00:05:31,046 --> 00:05:32,756
{\an8}[Karen] Chii, over here!

73
00:05:37,677 --> 00:05:39,095
You saved me a seat.

74
00:05:39,179 --> 00:05:42,474
Uh-huh. Right at the very center,
just like you asked for.

75
00:05:42,557 --> 00:05:44,601
Looks like they've got quite the crowd.

76
00:05:44,684 --> 00:05:47,979
At my school, hardly anybody showed up
for the play performances.

77
00:05:48,605 --> 00:05:50,315
Oh, look, it's Mr. Fortune Teller!

78
00:05:50,398 --> 00:05:51,441
Yes, greetings.

79
00:05:51,524 --> 00:05:52,734
[phone vibrating]

80
00:05:54,569 --> 00:05:56,821
[Haryu] One guy in my class said
he was coming

81
00:05:56,905 --> 00:05:59,199
just to see the rhythmic gymnastics girl.

82
00:05:59,282 --> 00:06:01,493
[Karen] Oh, so she must be
pretty cute, huh?

83
00:06:02,077 --> 00:06:04,037
{\an8}Who's cuter, me or her?

84
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:06,915
{\an8}Go on, young man, I don't mind.
You can tell me.

85
00:06:06,998 --> 00:06:08,583
{\an8}'Tis my lady Karen.

86
00:06:08,666 --> 00:06:10,502
{\an8}[Nishida] She's trained him well.

87
00:06:11,377 --> 00:06:13,797
I guess normally you don't go to a play

88
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:17,509
unless there's someone you want to see
or you know somebody in the cast.

89
00:06:17,592 --> 00:06:19,761
Is there anyone you know in the play?

90
00:06:20,345 --> 00:06:22,972
I don't know anyone.
But I know some people behind the scenes--

91
00:06:23,056 --> 00:06:24,516
- You know someone.
- [both] Mm?

92
00:06:24,599 --> 00:06:28,019
Taiki Inomata.
He's playing Prince Charming.

93
00:06:28,103 --> 00:06:29,270
{\an8}Our Taiki?

94
00:06:29,896 --> 00:06:31,064
{\an8}Prince Charming?

95
00:06:31,147 --> 00:06:33,274
{\an8}All of a sudden,
I'm really looking forward to this.

96
00:06:33,358 --> 00:06:35,401
{\an8}Make sure you've got your camera ready.

97
00:06:37,112 --> 00:06:38,279
[Nishida] Hm?

98
00:06:38,363 --> 00:06:40,949
{\an8}- How does Kano know he's in it?
- You two better be nice.

99
00:06:41,032 --> 00:06:43,785
{\an8}- Someone got injured, so he's standing in.
- It's love.

100
00:06:43,868 --> 00:06:45,995
- Word's getting around fast.
- [Karen sighs]

101
00:06:47,372 --> 00:06:50,333
TAIKI INOMATA
I'M GONNA BE IN THE PLAY! GO EASY ON ME!

102
00:06:50,416 --> 00:06:52,544
YOU GOT THIS!

103
00:06:57,632 --> 00:06:58,800
Hey, Imamoto.

104
00:06:59,509 --> 00:07:02,929
{\an8}Did you get the confetti ball set up
for the Best Class announcement?

105
00:07:03,012 --> 00:07:04,347
{\an8}Yeah, it's all set to go.

106
00:07:04,848 --> 00:07:07,434
{\an8}We barely managed
to finish it this morning,

107
00:07:07,517 --> 00:07:09,436
so it was a bit of a rush job
to hang it up.

108
00:07:09,519 --> 00:07:10,812
All right, good to hear.

109
00:07:12,147 --> 00:07:14,649
{\an8}Okay, the next performance up

110
00:07:14,732 --> 00:07:16,985
{\an8}is a play by the first-year students.

111
00:07:17,068 --> 00:07:21,281
{\an8}It seems that they've put their own
unique twist on a classic fairytale.

112
00:07:23,408 --> 00:07:24,951
[softly] I know this was unexpected,

113
00:07:25,034 --> 00:07:27,495
and I know anything can happen on stage.

114
00:07:27,579 --> 00:07:29,456
But let's do this and enjoy it!

115
00:07:29,539 --> 00:07:30,623
Let's go!

116
00:07:31,207 --> 00:07:32,584
[all, softly] Yeah!

117
00:07:34,669 --> 00:07:36,337
{\an8}Let's go, Taiki!

118
00:07:36,421 --> 00:07:38,006
{\an8}Don't give up, Taiki.

119
00:07:38,089 --> 00:07:39,299
{\an8}You can do it.

120
00:07:39,382 --> 00:07:41,593
{\an8}[Taiki] I feel like I'm about to play
a badminton match.

121
00:07:42,218 --> 00:07:44,304
<i>I went through the script once at least.</i>

122
00:07:44,387 --> 00:07:47,140
<i>As long as I don't freak out on stage,
I should be fine.</i>

123
00:07:48,558 --> 00:07:50,852
{\an8}I couldn't help
but imagine the real thing.

124
00:07:50,935 --> 00:07:52,479
{\an8}Kissing you for real, Taiki.

125
00:07:53,563 --> 00:07:57,484
<i>Come on. Would you
stop thinking about that?</i>

126
00:07:58,234 --> 00:08:01,070
- A prince wouldn't stand like that!
- [grunts]

127
00:08:01,988 --> 00:08:03,198
[grunts angrily]

128
00:08:05,158 --> 00:08:06,910
[Hina] Are you feeling nervous yet?

129
00:08:06,993 --> 00:08:08,745
{\an8}Well, give it up 'cause this is happening.

130
00:08:08,828 --> 00:08:12,499
{\an8}What do you mean "give it up"?
Are you telling me you don't get nervous?

131
00:08:13,082 --> 00:08:15,210
{\an8}Who do you think this is
standing in front of you?

132
00:08:15,293 --> 00:08:17,128
{\an8}I'm the great Hina Chono.

133
00:08:17,212 --> 00:08:18,755
[Taiki] Is that so?

134
00:08:19,339 --> 00:08:20,423
[sighs]

135
00:08:21,341 --> 00:08:23,510
[Hina] Yeah, of course, I'm nervous.

136
00:08:23,593 --> 00:08:24,511
[exclaims softly]

137
00:08:25,386 --> 00:08:29,516
It's way different from being in front
of people when I'm doing gymnastics.

138
00:08:29,599 --> 00:08:32,602
And then there's the fact
I wasn't expecting you to be my partner.

139
00:08:32,685 --> 00:08:33,895
[Taiki grunts softly]

140
00:08:35,230 --> 00:08:36,523
[Hina] But you know,

141
00:08:36,606 --> 00:08:38,191
{\an8}I was cast in the lead role,

142
00:08:38,274 --> 00:08:42,695
{\an8}so it gave me a sense of responsibility,
and I've been rehearsing non-stop.

143
00:08:42,779 --> 00:08:45,031
{\an8}- [Taiki] Mm-hm.
- [Hina] So that's why...

144
00:08:45,823 --> 00:08:47,534
I need you to really bring it.

145
00:08:47,617 --> 00:08:49,536
Be there as one of my closest friends.

146
00:08:51,621 --> 00:08:52,789
It's gonna be fine.

147
00:08:52,872 --> 00:08:56,251
<i>You'll never do anything more embarrassing
than that sports day.</i>

148
00:08:56,334 --> 00:08:58,795
[Taiki] <i>Hey, that was
part of the act we planned!</i>

149
00:08:58,878 --> 00:09:02,173
{\an8}Doesn't change the fact
it was terrible! [laughs]

150
00:09:02,257 --> 00:09:04,300
{\an8}We all had to participate!

151
00:09:04,384 --> 00:09:07,053
{\an8}Okay, then what about you in ninth grade?

152
00:09:07,136 --> 00:09:09,180
{\an8}I recall I was perfectly flawless!

153
00:09:10,390 --> 00:09:12,600
{\an8}Hey, guys, I'm back from the committee.

154
00:09:12,684 --> 00:09:15,061
- [boy] No, man, I'm positive!
- Hm?

155
00:09:15,144 --> 00:09:17,021
You think so?

156
00:09:17,105 --> 00:09:19,023
What are you guys talking about?

157
00:09:19,649 --> 00:09:23,987
[boy] Well, we were just wondering
if those two are going out! That's what.

158
00:09:24,070 --> 00:09:25,822
They've always been pretty tight.

159
00:09:25,905 --> 00:09:28,658
Uh, no, I'm pretty sure
they're just friends.

160
00:09:29,284 --> 00:09:31,202
[boy] Seriously? I mean, look at them.

161
00:09:32,704 --> 00:09:34,330
Yeah, you're not wrong.

162
00:09:34,414 --> 00:09:37,250
I wonder what the difference is
between platonic friends...

163
00:09:38,209 --> 00:09:39,586
and a relationship.

164
00:09:40,169 --> 00:09:42,130
[buzzer sounds]

165
00:09:42,839 --> 00:09:46,342
[host] <i>We now present</i>
Snow White <i>by Year 1 Class B.</i>

166
00:09:54,684 --> 00:09:55,935
{\an8}[classical music playing]

167
00:09:56,019 --> 00:09:57,478
{\an8}[narrator] <i>Once upon a time,</i>

168
00:09:58,313 --> 00:10:02,817
<i>the queen of the land gave birth
to a beautiful baby girl.</i>

169
00:10:04,611 --> 00:10:07,488
<i>Her skin was as white as fresh snow,</i>

170
00:10:08,114 --> 00:10:10,825
<i>and so, they called her Snow White.</i>

171
00:10:13,328 --> 00:10:15,371
[all exclaiming]

172
00:10:15,455 --> 00:10:17,749
<i>Snow White was cheerful and lively.</i>

173
00:10:18,374 --> 00:10:21,169
[Haryu] She is the rising star
of rhythmic gymnastics.

174
00:10:21,252 --> 00:10:22,754
She shines up there.

175
00:10:22,837 --> 00:10:25,256
[Karen] She looks
totally comfortable on stage.

176
00:10:28,134 --> 00:10:29,010
You there!

177
00:10:29,093 --> 00:10:31,512
Whatever are you doing
in a place like this?

178
00:10:32,221 --> 00:10:34,015
[Haryu and Nishida snickering]

179
00:10:34,682 --> 00:10:37,435
[Haryu] He's not making it a secret
that he's nervous.

180
00:10:37,518 --> 00:10:39,771
[Karen] He's not even walking naturally.

181
00:10:39,854 --> 00:10:43,149
But at least it's pretty obvious
he's giving it his all.

182
00:10:43,232 --> 00:10:44,400
[Chinatsu gasps softly]

183
00:10:46,110 --> 00:10:48,780
[Karen] Wait.
Was there always a scene in <i>Snow White</i>

184
00:10:48,863 --> 00:10:51,157
where the prince shows up this early?

185
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:53,284
[Haryu] I hear their adaptation's
pretty different.

186
00:10:53,368 --> 00:10:56,913
{\an8}Apparently, someone said
it didn't make sense for the princess

187
00:10:56,996 --> 00:10:59,499
{\an8}to end up with a guy
who showed up out of nowhere.

188
00:11:01,876 --> 00:11:05,213
So they added a scene at the beginning
where she meets the prince.

189
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:09,050
And that's when Snow White
falls in love with Prince Charming.

190
00:11:10,176 --> 00:11:14,055
They changed it so that at the end,
the kiss is from someone she loves.

191
00:11:14,138 --> 00:11:15,765
[gasps softly]

192
00:11:18,684 --> 00:11:20,812
[girl 1] Our version
turned out great, huh?

193
00:11:20,895 --> 00:11:24,649
[girl 2] I wouldn't wanna wake up being
kissed by someone I didn't know either.

194
00:11:24,732 --> 00:11:27,777
It would be nice to end up
with the one you've always loved.

195
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:29,112
How romantic!

196
00:11:29,195 --> 00:11:30,405
- [Ayame] Honestly?
- Huh?

197
00:11:31,948 --> 00:11:34,200
{\an8}If you ask me,
I'm not really into all that.

198
00:11:35,201 --> 00:11:38,162
{\an8}When you romanticize
long-time feelings for someone,

199
00:11:38,788 --> 00:11:40,706
{\an8}it really puts pressure on things.

200
00:11:41,666 --> 00:11:44,585
Don't you think casual relationships
are way more fun?

201
00:11:45,795 --> 00:11:48,172
Well, you're more uninhibited than us.

202
00:11:48,256 --> 00:11:50,842
[Ayame] Yeah, cause the rest of you
are way too serious!

203
00:11:50,925 --> 00:11:52,468
Come help us out for a while.

204
00:11:52,552 --> 00:11:55,346
[witch student] Beautiful young lady,
I have a gift for you.

205
00:11:55,430 --> 00:11:58,975
[Hina] Oh, my! What a beautiful apple!
Its skin is so red and glossy,

206
00:11:59,058 --> 00:12:01,477
its bottom is so plump,
and its form so pleasing.

207
00:12:01,561 --> 00:12:03,980
Indeed. I dare say
you're right, young miss!

208
00:12:04,063 --> 00:12:07,525
[Hina] It looks to be the sweetest apple
I've encountered in quite some time!

209
00:12:07,608 --> 00:12:09,235
We made it to the second half.

210
00:12:10,069 --> 00:12:10,987
[Taiki] Oh goodness...

211
00:12:11,070 --> 00:12:13,739
[boy] Taiki's really stressing himself out
over the kiss scene.

212
00:12:13,823 --> 00:12:15,491
[Kyo] Well, it is the big moment.

213
00:12:15,575 --> 00:12:16,993
So, Kyo, earlier,

214
00:12:17,076 --> 00:12:19,787
- what we were talking about...
- She appears too lifelike to be dead.

215
00:12:19,871 --> 00:12:23,416
[boy] You know, the difference between
platonic friends and a relationship.

216
00:12:23,499 --> 00:12:25,251
[Kyo] Oh. Yeah, I remember.

217
00:12:25,334 --> 00:12:28,129
My older brother told me
that the difference is...

218
00:12:28,713 --> 00:12:29,714
whether...

219
00:12:30,298 --> 00:12:32,216
[smooches] you'd kiss
the other person or not.

220
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:33,259
- [Taiki] Kiss?
- [coughs]

221
00:12:34,385 --> 00:12:36,429
Maybe keep your voice down a little?

222
00:12:36,512 --> 00:12:38,514
Oh, yeah, the audience might hear us.

223
00:12:39,098 --> 00:12:40,266
That, too, but...

224
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:44,270
[boy] My brother's a free spirit.
It's one person's opinion.

225
00:12:44,854 --> 00:12:48,649
But he says crossing the line
between friendship and relationship

226
00:12:48,733 --> 00:12:50,776
is about the all-important kiss.

227
00:12:51,861 --> 00:12:55,948
[Kyo] <i>If that's the standard, then, Taiki...</i>

228
00:12:56,032 --> 00:12:57,033
[Taiki] Hm?

229
00:12:57,116 --> 00:12:59,202
What are you guys talking about?

230
00:12:59,285 --> 00:13:00,536
Keep your nose out of it.

231
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:02,538
[Taiki] Wait, you're shutting me out?

232
00:13:04,916 --> 00:13:06,167
[shudders]

233
00:13:06,959 --> 00:13:10,213
{\an8}Right, right, right.
Now's the time to focus on the play!

234
00:13:11,047 --> 00:13:12,757
[dwarves crying]

235
00:13:14,133 --> 00:13:15,218
Goodness!

236
00:13:16,010 --> 00:13:18,554
Whatever has become of you, my Snow White?

237
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:22,183
She appears far too lifelike to be dead.

238
00:13:25,478 --> 00:13:27,605
<i>Hina asked me to do this for her,</i>

239
00:13:31,567 --> 00:13:33,444
{\an8}<i>as one of her closest friends.</i>

240
00:13:52,672 --> 00:13:55,466
[Hina gasps]

241
00:13:57,218 --> 00:13:58,761
Prince Charming!

242
00:14:00,346 --> 00:14:01,472
[exclaims softly]

243
00:14:02,807 --> 00:14:05,893
What's the big idea?
Are you trying to make a move on me?

244
00:14:05,977 --> 00:14:06,978
What?

245
00:14:07,061 --> 00:14:08,604
{\an8}Another part they changed.

246
00:14:08,688 --> 00:14:09,730
{\an8}She's brazen.

247
00:14:09,814 --> 00:14:12,775
[Taiki] <i>Good. It's almost over.</i>

248
00:14:12,859 --> 00:14:14,735
<i>Just the ending left now.</i>

249
00:14:15,611 --> 00:14:16,487
[exclaims softly]

250
00:14:20,449 --> 00:14:21,409
[gasps]

251
00:14:21,492 --> 00:14:22,660
Hina, watch out!

252
00:14:23,202 --> 00:14:24,245
[gasps]

253
00:14:35,006 --> 00:14:36,424
[all gasp]

254
00:14:45,975 --> 00:14:47,643
[grunts softly]

255
00:14:49,103 --> 00:14:50,563
[breath trembling]

256
00:14:52,565 --> 00:14:54,734
- [boy] Are you okay?
- [Imamoto] Anyone hurt?

257
00:14:54,817 --> 00:14:55,735
[all chattering]

258
00:14:55,818 --> 00:14:59,697
[host] Uh, please accept our apologies.
We're gonna take a brief intermission.

259
00:15:00,531 --> 00:15:03,326
{\an8}Did they actually just kiss?

260
00:15:03,409 --> 00:15:05,036
{\an8}[boy 2] I think you're imagining it.

261
00:15:05,119 --> 00:15:07,204
{\an8}[girl 1] You should be worried
rather than gossiping.

262
00:15:07,288 --> 00:15:09,040
{\an8}[girl 2] They got hit
by the confetti ball.

263
00:15:09,123 --> 00:15:10,207
{\an8}I wonder if they're okay.

264
00:15:10,291 --> 00:15:12,585
{\an8}[girl 3] That was Chono and a guy
from badminton, I think.

265
00:15:12,668 --> 00:15:14,420
{\an8}[girl 4] They hang out together a lot.

266
00:15:14,503 --> 00:15:15,630
They are dating, right?

267
00:15:15,713 --> 00:15:17,089
[girl 4] Mm, I don't think so.

268
00:15:27,266 --> 00:15:30,102
{\an8}I told you,
it wasn't an actual kiss, okay?

269
00:15:30,728 --> 00:15:33,356
With all the confetti,
I can see how it'd look like that.

270
00:15:33,439 --> 00:15:35,816
I got close to her,
but we didn't touch at all.

271
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:39,111
Look are you just saying that, man?
Or are you just embarrassed?

272
00:15:39,195 --> 00:15:41,238
Fess up, tell us the truth.

273
00:15:41,322 --> 00:15:42,823
I told you already!

274
00:15:42,907 --> 00:15:45,242
Well, Chono, is he telling the truth?

275
00:15:45,910 --> 00:15:46,994
{\an8}Yeah, he is.

276
00:15:47,078 --> 00:15:49,413
[boy 1] Oh. Okay, yeah.

277
00:15:50,331 --> 00:15:54,502
You must be aware, though. There's a rumor
making its way around the school

278
00:15:54,585 --> 00:15:56,253
that the two of you are actually dating.

279
00:15:56,337 --> 00:15:58,881
You are the prince and princess,
after all!

280
00:15:58,965 --> 00:16:01,717
[boy 2] Even without the accident,
people would talk.

281
00:16:01,801 --> 00:16:04,887
And really, you two had
great chemistry together on stage.

282
00:16:04,971 --> 00:16:09,350
[boy 1] So the people who saw the play
are probably thinking the rumor's true.

283
00:16:11,811 --> 00:16:14,438
I get it. I can see how
from your perspective

284
00:16:14,522 --> 00:16:16,399
it might've looked like a real kiss.

285
00:16:18,067 --> 00:16:20,695
{\an8}But the way that
you all are joking about it

286
00:16:20,778 --> 00:16:22,905
{\an8}is not funny, so please stop.

287
00:16:24,198 --> 00:16:25,282
I apologize.

288
00:16:25,366 --> 00:16:26,659
[gloomy music playing]

289
00:16:26,742 --> 00:16:27,952
[grunts]

290
00:16:34,542 --> 00:16:37,378
[Taiki] <i>I get the impulse to gossip. I do.</i>

291
00:16:39,088 --> 00:16:42,508
<i>But who I'm dating
is none of their business.</i>

292
00:16:43,426 --> 00:16:44,885
[Hina] Taiki!

293
00:16:49,015 --> 00:16:51,350
{\an8}Sorry about all the rumors.

294
00:16:52,018 --> 00:16:54,186
{\an8}It's not like it's your fault, Hina.

295
00:16:54,770 --> 00:16:56,188
{\an8}If anything, I'm sorry.

296
00:16:57,064 --> 00:16:58,941
{\an8}I couldn't make the play a success.

297
00:16:59,817 --> 00:17:01,193
{\an8}That isn't true at all!

298
00:17:01,777 --> 00:17:03,863
You remembered most of your lines.

299
00:17:03,946 --> 00:17:07,241
And you were nervous in the beginning,
but got better and better.

300
00:17:07,783 --> 00:17:09,410
You looked confident out there.

301
00:17:09,493 --> 00:17:12,246
Your voice carried. And... and...

302
00:17:13,164 --> 00:17:14,206
{\an8}and then when you...

303
00:17:14,790 --> 00:17:16,208
[exclaims]

304
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:20,463
You managed not to get overshadowed by me.

305
00:17:20,546 --> 00:17:21,714
I commend you!

306
00:17:21,797 --> 00:17:25,134
[Taiki] Well, then, as a thank-you,
how 'bout you do my homework?

307
00:17:25,217 --> 00:17:28,220
- [Hina] It'll be full of mistakes.
- [Taiki] Never mind then.

308
00:17:28,304 --> 00:17:31,474
- [chuckles]
- But, um, if you need me to...

309
00:17:32,058 --> 00:17:34,101
I can explain the situation.

310
00:17:34,185 --> 00:17:37,229
I can tell Chinatsu we didn't kiss,
just let me know!

311
00:17:37,313 --> 00:17:38,606
Huh?

312
00:17:38,689 --> 00:17:41,817
Well, you don't like
all of these rumors, right?

313
00:17:42,610 --> 00:17:46,781
It seemed like it made you pretty mad.
And I want this all to be fair!

314
00:17:48,324 --> 00:17:49,742
Oh, no, it wasn't...

315
00:17:53,871 --> 00:17:55,372
I wasn't upset about that.

316
00:17:58,959 --> 00:18:00,795
After-party in a bag.

317
00:18:01,545 --> 00:18:02,630
You must be tired.

318
00:18:03,339 --> 00:18:04,423
Thanks.

319
00:18:10,346 --> 00:18:12,139
Geez, someone's hungry.

320
00:18:12,223 --> 00:18:13,891
Gimme a break, just today!

321
00:18:14,767 --> 00:18:16,936
{\an8}Everyone's all, "Kiss this, kiss that."

322
00:18:17,019 --> 00:18:18,896
{\an8}Do they have nothing to say
about the play?

323
00:18:19,522 --> 00:18:21,857
As a stand-in, I did pretty well, right?

324
00:18:21,941 --> 00:18:23,150
[Kyo] Yeah, you did.

325
00:18:23,234 --> 00:18:26,195
[grunts] But then, what was up
with that confetti ball?

326
00:18:26,278 --> 00:18:27,988
What if someone had gotten hurt?

327
00:18:28,614 --> 00:18:30,658
[Kyo] <i>He's never in a bad mood.</i>

328
00:18:30,741 --> 00:18:32,618
[Taiki] And then there's Hina.

329
00:18:32,701 --> 00:18:36,413
She thinks Chinatsu is the only reason
I'm mad about it.

330
00:18:37,706 --> 00:18:38,791
Is it not?

331
00:18:40,751 --> 00:18:42,962
[Taiki] Well, that's part of it, but...

332
00:18:43,045 --> 00:18:46,924
more than anything, it's me and Hina
who are the ones being talked about.

333
00:18:48,050 --> 00:18:51,929
With Hina, I don't know where I stand
in our relationship these days.

334
00:18:52,555 --> 00:18:55,224
<i>So I get caught up
on how to act sometimes.</i>

335
00:18:55,307 --> 00:18:58,936
<i>I really hate people talking
about what we are.</i>

336
00:18:59,019 --> 00:19:02,773
{\an8}And, honestly, I kinda figured Hina
is probably feeling the same way.

337
00:19:03,524 --> 00:19:06,443
It seems like I'm the only one
who's mad, though.

338
00:19:08,404 --> 00:19:10,239
{\an8}I got a question, dude.

339
00:19:10,322 --> 00:19:11,198
Yeah.

340
00:19:12,241 --> 00:19:15,995
Are you not starting to have
feelings for Hina?

341
00:19:16,078 --> 00:19:17,621
[soft music playing]

342
00:19:19,123 --> 00:19:20,457
What?

343
00:19:20,541 --> 00:19:23,210
With how many times
she's approached you about it,

344
00:19:23,294 --> 00:19:25,337
it wouldn't be surprising if you are.

345
00:19:32,887 --> 00:19:34,722
The person I like...

346
00:19:35,806 --> 00:19:37,224
is Chinatsu.

347
00:19:38,893 --> 00:19:42,229
Of course, it is.
I mean, I get the vibe that

348
00:19:42,313 --> 00:19:45,316
{\an8}you're like 100% into Chinatsu.

349
00:19:45,399 --> 00:19:46,942
{\an8}But I feel like you might've added

350
00:19:47,026 --> 00:19:50,362
{\an8}an extra 30% or so of feelings
for Hina, you know?

351
00:19:53,574 --> 00:19:56,076
{\an8}I think that's completely plausible.

352
00:19:58,662 --> 00:19:59,997
That's all just...

353
00:20:00,664 --> 00:20:02,208
hypothetical, though.

354
00:20:04,877 --> 00:20:06,712
[groaning]

355
00:20:12,468 --> 00:20:14,011
My head's killing me.

356
00:20:15,221 --> 00:20:16,764
{\an8}No matter how much it hurts,

357
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:18,849
really think it through.

358
00:20:20,392 --> 00:20:21,477
[grunts]

359
00:20:24,063 --> 00:20:26,941
[announcer on PA]
<i>Everyone, thank you for your attendance.</i>

360
00:20:27,608 --> 00:20:30,611
That was a girl back there,
so I still have a chance.

361
00:20:30,694 --> 00:20:31,779
[boy] Keep it movin'.

362
00:20:31,862 --> 00:20:35,157
{\an8}Do people from Kansai
eat <i>takoyaki</i> with rice?

363
00:20:36,367 --> 00:20:39,161
It's that guy
who kissed the girl in the play.

364
00:20:40,371 --> 00:20:42,915
- [announcer] <i>Now, we officially bring...</i>
- Really?

365
00:20:42,998 --> 00:20:43,958
EIMEI FESTIVAL

366
00:20:44,041 --> 00:20:47,169
{\an8}<i>...the 53rd Eimei Cultural Festival
to a close.</i>

367
00:20:58,847 --> 00:21:01,100
{\an8}[Taiki] 100% coffee.

368
00:21:03,018 --> 00:21:04,728
Thirty percent milk.

369
00:21:09,817 --> 00:21:11,068
<i>Tasty.</i>

370
00:21:11,151 --> 00:21:14,697
<i>So it's possible to have a mixture
of feelings for both of them?</i>

371
00:21:15,614 --> 00:21:16,782
[exclaims]

372
00:21:16,865 --> 00:21:19,285
<i>Wait, no, that can't be!</i>

373
00:21:20,869 --> 00:21:21,954
[sighs]

374
00:21:22,037 --> 00:21:24,373
<i>Why does Kyo gotta say weird stuff?</i>

375
00:21:24,957 --> 00:21:27,042
<i>The one I have a crush on is Chinatsu.</i>

376
00:21:27,126 --> 00:21:28,294
[groans, spits coffee]

377
00:21:28,377 --> 00:21:29,920
[coughs]

378
00:21:30,004 --> 00:21:31,797
Chinatsu, what are you doing here?

379
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:32,923
You're in my house?

380
00:21:34,508 --> 00:21:36,677
My grandpa's doing well after his surgery.

381
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:39,179
So I'll be staying here again
starting tomorrow.

382
00:21:39,263 --> 00:21:40,723
I came to bring some stuff.

383
00:21:40,806 --> 00:21:43,183
[Taiki] <i>I guess I knew
she was coming back soon.</i>

384
00:21:43,267 --> 00:21:45,436
Thanks again for taking me in, Taiki.

385
00:21:45,519 --> 00:21:47,187
Uh, you're welcome.

386
00:21:49,606 --> 00:21:51,692
<i>Chinatsu saw what happened, too.</i>

387
00:21:59,825 --> 00:22:01,952
<i>I wonder what she thinks about it.</i>

388
00:22:05,581 --> 00:22:07,583
[closing theme song playing]
